…\n  ECDSAKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — An ECDSA (NIST P-curve) key — from_private_key_file(path) or generate().\n  Ed25519Key(path=None, password=None, _data=None, **kw) — An Ed25519 key — the default modern host and user key type.\n  HostKeys(filename=None) — A known_hosts database — load, add, lookup, save; what a MissingHostKeyPolicy decides on.\n  IncompatiblePeer(...) — The peer offers no algorithm in common — no shared kex, cipher, MAC or host key type.\n  InteractiveQuery(name='', instructions='', *prompts) — Server side: the prompt set returned by keyboard-interactive authentication.\n  Message(content=None) — An SSH wire message being built or read — get_/add_ one typed field at a time.\n  MessageOrderError(...) — A protocol message arrived out of the order the SSH state machine allows.\n  MissingHostKeyPolicy() — Base policy for an unknown host key — subclass and implement missing_host_key().\n  NoValidConnectionsError(errors=None) — Every candidate address for that host refused the connection.\n  PKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — Base of every key type: from_private_key_file/from_private_key, generate, get_fingerprint.\n  PasswordRequiredException(...) — The private key is encrypted and no passphrase was given to load it.\n  ProxyCommand(command_line) — A local command used as the transport socket — ProxyCommand from an ssh_config.\n  ProxyCommandFailure(...) — The ProxyCommand process failed or closed before the session was up.\n  PublicBlob(type_, blob, comment=None) — A raw public-key blob (an OpenSSH certificate or `.pub` body), from_string/from_file.\n  RSAKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — An RSA private or public key — from_private_key_file(path, password=None) or generate(bi…\n  RejectPolicy() — Refuse to connect to a host whose key is not already known. The safe default.\n  SFTP(handle) — SFTP over an open Transport: listdir, stat, open, get/put, mkdir, remove, rename.\n  SFTPAttributes() — Stat of one remote pa